  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nSurface high pressure will drift east across the region through\nSunday, maintaining dry weather. Mid and high clouds are \nexpected to increase in warm advection ahead of a weakening \nshortwave trough across the Midwest. This trough is progged to\ncross the Upper Ohio Valley region on Monday, though with\ndiminishing ascent and a lack of deep layer moisture, a dry\nforecast was maintained. \n\nModel ensembles indicate ridging will build across the Upper\nOhio Valley region again Tuesday, with decreased clouds, dry\nweather, and likely the warmest temperatures of the week. A\ntrough across the central CONUS is then expected to advance\neastward on Wednesday, approaching and crossing the region \nlate Wednesday and Thursday. This is expected to bring\nincreasing rain chances, with the highest POPs currently on\nThursday. Lingering broad upper troughing should keep rain\nchances in the forecast at times Friday and Saturday.",
